    "sections": [
      {
        "label": "1st quarter",
        "score": "NE 3, MIA 3",
        "text": "Andy Borregales opened the scoring with a 34-yard field goal. Jacob Rodriguez then forced an Efton Chism III fumble that Miami recovered at the New England 19, and Zane Gonzalez's 31-yard field goal tied it 3–3."
      },
      {
        "label": "2nd quarter",
        "score": "MIA 13, NE 3",
        "text": "Gonzalez's 52-yarder bounced in off the upright for a 6–3 Miami lead. Borregales missed a 40-yard try wide right with 2:24 left, and Miami answered with an 11-play, 70-yard drive capped by Malik Willis's 1-yard touchdown pass to Malik Washington with eight seconds left. Hunter Henry left with a foot injury."
      },
      {
        "label": "3rd quarter",
        "score": "NE 17, MIA 13",
        "text": "Maye hit Kyle Williams for a 43-yard touchdown that was ruled incomplete until Mike Vrabel's challenge overturned it, making it 13–10. Maye then scored on a 2-yard run off a fake pitch on third-and-goal with 59 seconds left. He went 7-of-7 for 96 yards in the quarter."
      },
      {
        "label": "4th quarter",
        "score": "Final: NE 24, MIA 19",
        "text": "Kevin Byard's first interception as a Patriot set up Maye's 48-yard touchdown to DeMario Douglas for a 24–13 lead with 12:39 left. Willis found Kevin Coleman Jr. for a 35-yard score with 2:04 left, but the two-point try failed, Rhamondre Stevenson recovered the onside kick, and his 5-yard run on third-and-5 ran out the clock."
      }
    ],
